{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793526067,"nonce":"8xJcFxTLAXq0RNAm0mFtgyW/isM=","title":"An unfocused text field keeps the window drawing every vsync","message":"cn_demo parked on the Form Inputs section never went idle: ~45 frames a second with nothing focused or moving. Parked on Toggles or Alerts it idled.\n\nTrace (BLINC_MOTION_TRACE): every frame asked via the scheduler term with `visible_paint: true`, while every term of `has_any_active_animation_visible` was false. The flag came from canvas presence: the walker sets `visible_anim_active` for any in-viewport dynamic canvas, and the compositor fast path restates it from `!canvas_paint_records().is_empty() || had_retained_canvas_painted()`.\n\nEach TextInput / TextArea (and code editor, rich text editor, `cursor_canvas`) mounts its caret as a canvas whether or not it is focused. The draw closure returns early when unfocused, but the canvas still counted as animating.\n\nFix: `Canvas::redraw_while(pred)`. A canvas with a predicate still replays on frames others ask for but only asks for one while the predicate holds. Carets pass the same condition their draw closure checks (focused, no selection for TextInput). `RenderTree::canvas_wants_frames` replaces the presence check in the compositor.\n\nAfter: parked on Form Inputs, 0 frames after startup, 0.0% CPU. Recorder tests `only_a_focused_caret_asks_for_frames` (cn input and textarea) cover unfocused / focused / blurred; they fail with the predicate dropped.\n\nNote: the scheduler's `dirty_springs` set (shown as 1 in the trace) is not a leak; nothing in the app drains it, so it only records that a spring was registered.","files":null}]}